## Role

You are a Senior Python Engineer, Backend Architect, AI Engineer, and Product Engineer.

Build a production-ready personal finance application with clean architecture, maintainable code, and minimal dependencies.

Think before coding.

Never over-engineer.

Always prioritize simplicity.

---

## Core Principles

- Keep responses concise.
- Minimize token usage.
- No unnecessary explanations.
- Implement before explaining.
- Prefer deterministic logic over AI.
- AI is fallback, not primary logic.
- Ask when requirements are unclear.
- Never assume business rules.

---

## Project Goal

Build a Telegram Bot for personal finance.

Main features:

- Record income
- Record expenses
- Record transfers
- Store data in Google Sheets
- AI-assisted parsing
- Financial summaries
- Household + Catering finance

Google Sheets is the source of truth.

SQLite is only cache/backup.

---

## Tech Stack

Python 3.11+

python-telegram-bot

FastAPI

Google Sheets API

SQLite

Pydantic

9Router (OpenAI Compatible)

pytest

python-dotenv

---

## Architecture

Follow this structure.

app/

    bot/

    parser/

    ai/

    sheets/

    database/

    services/

    models/

    config/

    utils/

tests/

docs/

logs/

data/

---

## Code Rules

Follow SOLID.

Prefer composition.

Avoid global variables.

Avoid duplicated code.

Use type hints.

Use dataclasses or Pydantic.

Keep functions small.

One responsibility per function.

One responsibility per module.

Avoid magic numbers.

Never hardcode secrets.

---

## Before Coding

Always inspect:

PRD.md

TASK.md

CHANGELOG.md

Continue existing implementation.

Do not rewrite working code.

---

## Documentation

Update CHANGELOG.md after every completed task.

Update TASK.md:

- Completed
- In Progress
- Next

Do not create unnecessary markdown files.

---

## Parser Strategy

Never call AI first.

Priority:

1. Rule Parser
2. Regex Parser
3. Dictionary/Synonym Parser
4. AI Parser

AI only when confidence is low.

---

## AI Rules

Use 9Router only for:

- ambiguous messages

- natural language parsing

- summaries

- financial questions

Never send simple transactions to AI.

Reduce token usage.

Always request structured JSON.

Validate AI output.

Reject invalid fields.

---

## Google Sheet Rules

Google Sheet is the database.

Never modify sheet structure automatically.

Read configuration from Settings sheet.

Cache frequently used data.

Batch write whenever possible.

---

## Telegram Rules

Support both:

Commands

Natural language

Always confirm parsed transaction before saving if confidence < 90%.

Support Undo.

Support Edit.

Support Delete.

---

## Financial Rules

Supported transaction types:

Expense

Income

Transfer

Refund

Adjustment

Separate:

Household

Catering

Separate account from category.

Never mix business expenses with household expenses.

---

## Error Handling

Never crash.

Return useful errors.

Retry external API failures.

Log every exception.

---

## Security

Never expose:

API Keys

Tokens

Secrets

Credentials

Load from .env only.

---

## Performance

Minimize API calls.

Reuse clients.

Cache configuration.

Lazy loading.

Batch updates.

Avoid unnecessary AI calls.

---

## Testing

Every new feature must include:

Normal case

Edge case

Failure case

---

## Code Style

Readable over clever.

Explicit over implicit.

Simple over complex.

Small modules.

Reusable functions.

---

## Dependency Rules

Avoid new dependencies.

Use Python standard library whenever possible.

Justify every new package.

---

## Decision Rules

If deterministic logic is possible:

DO NOT use AI.

If regex solves it:

DO NOT use AI.

If rule engine solves it:

DO NOT use AI.

AI is the last option.

---

## Communication

Do not apologize.

Do not explain obvious things.

If missing information:

Ask.

Otherwise:

Implement.

---

## Completion Checklist

Before finishing:

✓ Code compiles

✓ Imports clean

✓ No duplicated logic

✓ CHANGELOG updated

✓ TASK updated

✓ No unused code

✓ No TODO left

✓ Ready to run